/-!
# Unitary CM–arithmetic interaction conjugated by the exact original causal shear

The ACTUAL degree-zero full-variety CM Thom/Betti source, with its existing
chosen positive coordinate metric, supplies the normalized geometric vector.
The ACTUAL integer-labelled original Mobius latent+response vector at time
zero supplies the normalized arithmetic vector, including mu(1)=1 and ALL
other labels, squareful zeros and signs.

Their previously constructed rank-two K=|w><v|+|v><w| is self-adjoint.
For a SEPARATELY SPECIFIED real coupling strength κ, let

      Rκ(s,t) = exp (-i κ (t-s) K).

This is a unitary, exactly composable interaction on the full joint Hilbert
space, unlike the earlier polynomial shear frame. Let E(s,t) denote the
original bounded, label-preserving causal Mobius response cocycle. Define

      Uκ(s,t) = E(0,t) Rκ(s,t) E(s,0).

Then Uκ(t,u)Uκ(s,t)=Uκ(s,u) on the entire joint Hilbert space, and κ=0
returns the old decoupled arithmetic transport. For nonnegative s,t,
‖Uκ(s,t)‖ ≤ 25 independently of s,t,κ and finite inventory j, because the
unitary interaction has norm one and the two causal shears cost ≤5 each.

The unitary Rκ is generated by the selected bounded self-adjoint K; the
full Uκ need NOT be unitary because actual pickup responses are born at
nonzero times. The coupling strength, action, dimensional units, physical
polarization, and identification of this operator with a physical PDE are
NOT supplied. Uniform bounds on the COHERENT signed arithmetic energy and
Schwartz-to-periodic local smoothing are separate, still-open problems.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
noncomputable section

